00:02:06,235 --> 00:02:08,032
{ MRS. FISHER SCREAMS }

10
00:02:09,915 --> 00:02:12,190
MRS. FISHER : My babies !

11
00:02:13,875 --> 00:02:15,707
{ CONTINUES SCREAMING }

12
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,034
Arthur ?

13
00:03:53,041 --> 00:03:54,633


14
00:03:57,961 --> 00:03:59,599
JOSEPH : Daddy ?

15
00:03:59,681 --> 00:04:01,319
Coming .

16
00:04:02,001 --> 00:04:03,070


17
00:04:08,001 --> 00:04:09,481
{ LOCKING BRIEFCASE }

18
00:04:13,442 --> 00:04:15,194
Do you like it , Daddy ?

19
00:04:16,522 --> 00:04:18,035
Very much .

20
00:04:19,722 --> 00:04:21,599
You didn 't look at it properly .

21
00:04:21,682 --> 00:04:23,195
Of course I did .

22
00:04:24,842 --> 00:04:27,641
That 's me , that 's Nanny ,

23
00:04:27,723 --> 00:04:31,511
that 's Mummy , and that 's you .

24
00:04:33,203 --> 00:04:34,602
Why do I look so sad ?

25
00:04:34,683 --> 00:04:37,436
That 's what your face looks like .

26
00:04:37,523 --> 00:04:39,514
ARTHUR : Oh , it is , is it ?

27
00:04:40,283 --> 00:04:42,922
I wish you didn 't have to go away from me .

28
00:04:44,123 --> 00:04:45,112
Me , too .

29
00:04:45,203 --> 00:04:47,638
But we 'll have the whole weekend

30
00:04:47,724 --> 00:04:48,918
in the countryside , won 't we ?

31
00:04:49,004 --> 00:04:50,995
See , tomorrow ,

32
00:04:52,164 --> 00:04:53,916
then Thursday ,

33
00:04:54,964 --> 00:04:56,642
and then we 're back together .

34
00:04:56,668 --> 00:04:57,708
Not long at all .

35
00:05:03,284 --> 00:05:05,719
You look just like your mother .

36
00:05:06,885 --> 00:05:07,874
Have you got the train tickets ?

37
00:05:07,965 --> 00:05:09,159
Yes , we 've got the train tickets .

38
00:05:09,245 --> 00:05:10,344
And you know all the times ?

39
00:05:10,370 --> 00:05:11,386
Yes , we know the times .

40
00:05:11,885 --> 00:05:13,414
Okay , I 've got to go .

41
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:15,186
Don 't want to be late .

42
00:05:15,245 --> 00:05:16,224
Go , we 'll be fine .

43
00:05:16,250 --> 00:05:17,500
We 'll see you Friday .

44
00:05:17,565 --> 00:05:19,954
See you . Wave bye-bye .

45
00:05:27,926 --> 00:05:30,235
I know you 've had it rough , Kipps ,

46
00:05:30,326 --> 00:05:34,114
and I 'm sympathetic to your situation .

47
00:05:36,846 --> 00:05:39,440
But we can 't carry passengers .

48
00:05:40,446 --> 00:05:43,803
We 're a law firm , not a charity .

49
00:05:46,047 --> 00:05:47,321
Good .

50
00:05:47,407 --> 00:05:49,682
I take it Tomes has briefed you

51
00:05:49,767 --> 00:05:54,636
on Mrs. Alice Drablow of Eel Marsh House .

52
00:05:54,727 --> 00:05:57,525
Died . Last month .

53
00:05:57,607 --> 00:06:00,519
Years since I went there , of course .

54
00:06:00,607 --> 00:06:04,760
The old widow didn 't greatly care for visitors .

55
00:06:05,768 --> 00:06:06,803
No children ?

56
00:06:09,128 --> 00:06:11,961
A boy . Died young .

57
00:06:12,848 --> 00:06:14,600
Many years ago .

58
00:06:14,688 --> 00:06:16,326
I 'll let you have the details

59
00:06:16,408 --> 00:06:18,046
to read on your journey .

60
00:06:18,128 --> 00:06:19,880
But , principally , you 're going to go through

61
00:06:19,968 --> 00:06:21,641
Mrs. Drablow 's documents .

62
00:06:22,249 --> 00:06:24,809
Make sure we 've got her final will .

63
00:06:24,889 --> 00:06:27,244
There 's a mountain of paperwork at the house .

64
00:06:27,329 --> 00:06:29,399
It all needs to be gone through . Every page .

65
00:06:29,489 --> 00:06:30,558
Very good .

66
00:06:30,649 --> 00:06:33,243
We 've been dealing with a local man , Jerome .

67
00:06:33,329 --> 00:06:35,797
But he 's not really been cooperating .

68
00:06:38,809 --> 00:06:40,926
What I 'm hoping , Kipps ,

69
00:06:41,010 --> 00:06:43,399
is that you 'll seize this chance

70
00:06:43,490 --> 00:06:45,242
to prove your dedication

71
00:06:45,330 --> 00:06:48,367
to pursuing a future with this firm .

72
00:06:49,810 --> 00:06:52,643
This is your final warning .

73
00:07:16,091 --> 00:07:17,525
{ STELLA SCREAMS }

74
00:07:21,932 --> 00:07:23,604
{ STELLA CONTINUES SCREAMING }

75
00:07:35,372 --> 00:07:36,806
GIRL : Mummy ?

76
00:07:36,893 --> 00:07:39,532
Mummy . My darling .

77
00:07:47,653 --> 00:07:49,723
{ RAIN PATTERING }

78
00:07:58,414 --> 00:08:00,245


79
00:08:18,695 --> 00:08:20,094
DOCTOR : Mr. Kipps .

80
00:08:24,135 --> 00:08:25,773
It 's a boy .

81
00:08:32,936 --> 00:08:34,574
{ LAUGHS SOFTLY }

82
00:08:38,336 --> 00:08:40,327
I 'm very sorry , Mr. Kipps .

83
00:08:51,417 --> 00:08:55,012
{ TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWS }

84
00:09:03,657 --> 00:09:05,648
Have we passed Crythin Gifford yet ?

85
00:09:06,217 --> 00:09:07,730
Next stop .

86
00:09:13,538 --> 00:09:15,972
So , you 're up from London ?

87
00:09:16,058 --> 00:09:17,286
I am .

88
00:09:17,898 --> 00:09:20,332
Trying to sell Eel Marsh House ?

89
00:09:23,218 --> 00:09:25,254
You won 't find a local buyer .

90
00:09:30,019 --> 00:09:31,338
Are you staying at The Gifford Arms ?

91
00:09:31,419 --> 00:09:32,568
Yes .

92
00:09:33,019 --> 00:09:34,418
It 's a bit of a walk from the station .

93
00:09:34,499 --> 00:09:35,898
I can give you a lift .

94
00:09:35,979 --> 00:09:37,412
It 's on my way home .

95
00:09:37,499 --> 00:09:39,217
Thank you .

96
00:09:39,699 --> 00:09:41,815
Samuel Daily .

97
00:09:41,899 --> 00:09:43,332
Arthur Kipps .

98
00:09:45,259 --> 00:09:47,136
ARTHUR : It 's a beautiful car , Mr. Daily .

99
00:09:47,219 --> 00:09:49,150
DAILY : First one in the county .

100
00:09:49,176 --> 00:09:50,794
Still scares the locals .

101
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:52,009
Here we are .

102
00:09:52,620 --> 00:09:54,690
Well , thank you .

103
00:09:56,420 --> 00:09:58,456
Very good to talk to you , Mr. Daily .

104
00:10:01,980 --> 00:10:03,208
Mr. Kipps ?

105
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:04,849
Would you like to have supper

106
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:06,532
with my wife and me tomorrow evening ?

107
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:08,816
You know , we don 't get to see many new faces here .

108
00:10:08,941 --> 00:10:10,215
Besides , the food in there ,

109
00:10:10,301 --> 00:10:11,859
reckon even a dog wouldn 't eat it .

110
00:10:11,941 --> 00:10:13,260
That 'd be lovely . Thank you .

111
00:10:13,341 --> 00:10:15,013
Night .

112
00:10:21,021 --> 00:10:22,500
ARTHUR : Good evening .

113
00:10:22,621 --> 00:10:25,534
I 've a room booked until Sunday . Mr. Kipps .

114
00:10:29,102 --> 00:10:31,252
No , I 'm not finding any booking .

115
00:10:31,342 --> 00:10:32,821
My office had telegraphed ahead .

116
00:10:32,902 --> 00:10:35,211
Well , we 're packed to the rafters . So ...

117
00:10:38,062 --> 00:10:39,541
Evening . Good evening .

118
00:10:39,622 --> 00:10:42,261
I was just telling Mr. Kipps that we don 't have any room .

119
00:10:44,302 --> 00:10:47,056
Well , we can 't have him out in this weather , can we ?

120
00:10:47,143 --> 00:10:48,417
Not in the rain .

121
00:10:49,663 --> 00:10:51,813
We must have something , just for tonight .

122
00:10:51,943 --> 00:10:53,501
We don 't .

123
00:10:55,103 --> 00:10:56,422
Unless you want to put him in the attic ?

124
00:10:59,303 --> 00:11:00,338
Fine .

125
00:11:05,304 --> 00:11:06,976
It 's this way .

126
00:11:15,504 --> 00:11:17,381


127
00:11:18,704 --> 00:11:20,422
Actually , I was hoping to stay till the weekend .

128
00:11:20,504 --> 00:11:22,894
My son and his nanny are traveling up to join me .

129
00:11:23,705 --> 00:11:25,377
Oh , I see .

130
00:11:28,145 --> 00:11:29,817
If a holiday is what you 're after , sir ,

131
00:11:29,905 --> 00:11:32,703
you 'd honestly be better off further inland .

132
00:11:32,785 --> 00:11:34,901
It gets awfully cold here , what with the sea mists .

133
00:11:34,985 --> 00:11:38,295
BIRD : Sea mist . Sea mist .

134
00:11:40,105 --> 00:11:41,744
It 's this way .

135
00:11:51,986 --> 00:11:53,339
How old is your son ?

136
00:11:53,466 --> 00:11:54,899
He 's four .

137
00:11:54,986 --> 00:11:56,499
Lovely age .

138
00:12:05,707 --> 00:12:07,186
Thank you .

139
00:12:19,068 --> 00:12:20,626
Goodnight .

140
00:12:35,748 --> 00:12:37,740
{ WINDOWS RATTLING }

141
00:13:00,750 --> 00:13:02,183
In .

142
00:13:45,752 --> 00:13:46,821
Hello ?

143
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:04,863
Mrs. Jerome ?

144
00:14:04,953 --> 00:14:06,750
Mr. Kipps ? Yes .

145
00:14:08,273 --> 00:14:10,548
My husband went to meet you at The Gifford Arms .

146
00:14:10,633 --> 00:14:11,827
{ DOOR OPENS }

147
00:14:14,314 --> 00:14:16,828
This is Mr. Kipps .

148
00:14:17,994 --> 00:14:19,143
I made it clear to your firm

149
00:14:19,234 --> 00:14:21,065
that there was no need for you to make the journey .

150
00:14:21,154 --> 00:14:22,382
We could have sent all the relevant documents

151
00:14:22,474 --> 00:14:23,543
to London .

152
00:14:23,634 --> 00:14:24,703
In any event ,

153
00:14:24,834 --> 00:14:27,348
you 'll find all the legal papers in here .

154
00:14:28,314 --> 00:14:30,305
Mr. Fisher tells me you 're leaving today .

155
00:14:31,115 --> 00:14:34,585
Not until I 've taken care of all Mrs. Drablow 's paperwork .

156
00:14:34,675 --> 00:14:35,790
All in there , as I said .

157
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:36,990
No , at the house .

158
00:14:37,075 --> 00:14:38,793
I 'm told there 's quite a substantial amount .

159
00:14:38,875 --> 00:14:42,151
I don 't expect to be finished until Friday , at least .

160
00:14:45,075 --> 00:14:46,713
It 's not possible .

161
00:14:47,395 --> 00:14:48,987
The Gifford Arms is fully booked for the week .

162
00:14:51,636 --> 00:14:53,911
I shall have to contact my office .

163
00:14:54,916 --> 00:14:56,588
Do you have a telephone ?

164
00:14:56,676 --> 00:14:58,792
Not even Mr. Daily has a telephone , sir .

165
00:14:58,876 --> 00:15:00,355
You 'll not find one in Crythin Gifford .

166
00:15:00,436 --> 00:15:01,664
Fine . I 'll send a telegram .

167
00:15:02,956 --> 00:15:05,516
The Post Office is closed on Wednesday morning .

168
00:15:05,596 --> 00:15:07,314
The London train leaves in half an hour .

169
00:15:07,396 --> 00:15:08,955
My colleague , Keckwick , is waiting outside

170
00:15:09,037 --> 00:15:10,629
with your luggage .

171
00:15:10,757 --> 00:15:13,510
It 's a pleasure to meet you , Mr. Kipps .

172
00:15:27,558 --> 00:15:29,514
Mr. Keckwick , a change of plans .

173
00:15:29,598 --> 00:15:30,713
I 'm not catching the train .

174
00:15:30,798 --> 00:15:32,231
You 'll take me to Eel Marsh House .

175
00:15:32,318 --> 00:15:34,832
Jerome paid me to take you to the station .

176
00:15:37,678 --> 00:15:38,667
{ COINS JINGLING }

177
00:15:42,718 --> 00:15:44,549
Make it six and I 'll think about it .

178
00:15:44,638 --> 00:15:45,912
Six shillings ?

179
00:15:46,519 --> 00:15:49,511
You 'll not find anyone else willing to take you there .

180
00:17:01,082 --> 00:17:02,721
There you are .

181
00:17:10,643 --> 00:17:12,838
Can you pick me up at 3 : 00 ? I can 't .

182
00:17:12,923 --> 00:17:13,958
I need to get back to the mainland

183
00:17:14,043 --> 00:17:15,158
before the tide comes in ,

184
00:17:15,243 --> 00:17:17,279
else I 'll be stuck here for the day .

185
00:17:17,363 --> 00:17:18,951
It will be out again by 5 : 00 .

186
00:17:18,977 --> 00:17:20,620
I 'll come back for you then .

187
00:17:20,684 --> 00:17:22,322
5 : 00 then .

188
00:18:33,447 --> 00:18:35,563
{ DOOR UNLOCKS }

189
00:19:48,971 --> 00:19:50,643


190
00:21:31,697 --> 00:21:33,608
{ MUFFLED THUD }

191
00:21:34,257 --> 00:21:36,054
{ THUDDING CONTINUES }

192
00:22:22,019 --> 00:22:24,773
{ SOFT THUDDING }

193
00:22:59,981 --> 00:23:01,335
{ DOOR RATTLES }

194
00:24:00,665 --> 00:24:02,417


195
00:24:05,785 --> 00:24:07,423
{ GLASS BREAKING }

196
00:24:08,705 --> 00:24:09,933
Come on , then .

197
00:24:30,426 --> 00:24:32,098


198
00:24:58,388 --> 00:24:59,741
Hello ?

199
00:25:06,228 --> 00:25:08,139
{ HORSE NEIGHS }

200
00:25:13,509 --> 00:25:15,340
{ WOMAN SCREAMS }

201
00:25:19,229 --> 00:25:21,299
{ HORSE NEIGHS }

202
00:25:21,389 --> 00:25:23,380
{ CARRIAGE RUMBLING }

203
00:25:26,469 --> 00:25:27,982
{ EERIE VOICES MURMURING }

204
00:25:33,270 --> 00:25:34,669
Who 's there ?

205
00:25:38,750 --> 00:25:40,706
{ BREATHING HEAVILY }

206
00:25:42,430 --> 00:25:44,739
{ BOY SHOUTING }

207
00:25:53,951 --> 00:25:55,020
MAN : Get the boy !

208
00:25:55,111 --> 00:25:56,100
Keckwick !

209
00:25:56,191 --> 00:25:57,180


210
00:26:01,591 --> 00:26:02,944
{ BREATHING HEAVILY }

211
00:26:03,031 --> 00:26:04,384
Mummy !

212
00:26:06,431 --> 00:26:07,830
MAN : Get the boy !

213
00:26:30,953 --> 00:26:33,786
ARTHUR : Constable , I 'm telling you , I heard an accident .

214
00:26:34,193 --> 00:26:37,742
No one has used Nine Lives Causeway for years , sir .

215
00:26:38,353 --> 00:26:40,150
Not since the little Drablow boy

216
00:26:40,273 --> 00:26:42,264
was drowned in the marshes .

217
00:26:42,673 --> 00:26:44,823
Eel Marsh House , it 's empty .

218
00:26:44,913 --> 00:26:46,038
It 's not , though .

219
00:26:46,064 --> 00:26:47,453
I saw a woman there .

220
00:26:52,434 --> 00:26:54,743
Excuse me one moment , sir .

221
00:26:57,354 --> 00:26:58,343
{ DOOR OPENS }

222
00:27:05,995 --> 00:27:08,668
Sir , my sister needs help .

223
00:27:09,995 --> 00:27:10,855
What 's the matter ?

224
00:27:10,881 --> 00:27:12,170
What 's your name , darling ?

225
00:27:12,235 --> 00:27:13,554
Her name is Victoria Hardy .

226
00:27:13,635 --> 00:27:14,750
What happened , Victoria ?

227
00:27:14,835 --> 00:27:16,028
Did something bad happen ?

228
00:27:16,054 --> 00:27:17,055
She drank some lye .

229
00:27:17,115 --> 00:27:18,707
Our mum was out .

230
00:27:19,595 --> 00:27:22,155
Lye . Oh , God . Constable !

231
00:27:22,275 --> 00:27:24,551
Is she going to die ? Constable !

232
00:27:24,636 --> 00:27:25,751
It 's going to be all right .

233
00:27:25,836 --> 00:27:27,235
Darling , just let me look at you ...

234
00:27:33,476 --> 00:27:34,670
Constable !

235
00:27:39,436 --> 00:27:41,313
{ CHURCH BELLS TOLLING }

236
00:27:44,117 --> 00:27:45,391
{ MRS. HARDY SCREAMS }

237
00:27:47,317 --> 00:27:49,672
MRS. HARDY : No !

238
00:27:50,757 --> 00:27:54,989
No , my baby !

239
00:28:11,718 --> 00:28:13,356


240
00:28:42,440 --> 00:28:44,271
{ FAINT SOBBING }

241
00:28:48,320 --> 00:28:50,197
{ SOBBING GROWS LOUDER }

242
00:28:52,240 --> 00:28:53,559
Hello ?

243
00:28:54,280 --> 00:28:56,111
Mrs. Fisher ?

244
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:57,792
{ SOBBING CONTINUES }

245
00:29:07,561 --> 00:29:09,791


246
00:29:32,842 --> 00:29:34,355
It 's getting late .

247
00:29:34,442 --> 00:29:35,921
You 'll miss your London train .

248
00:29:38,043 --> 00:29:39,601
I can 't leave yet .

249
00:29:40,843 --> 00:29:43,596
Please don 't go back to Eel Marsh House .

250
00:29:44,003 --> 00:29:44,992
Why ?

251
00:29:46,163 --> 00:29:50,156
Mr. Kipps , you said you have a son ?

252
00:29:50,243 --> 00:29:51,756
Yes .

253
00:29:52,443 --> 00:29:54,320
Go home to him .

254
00:29:54,843 --> 00:29:58,314
Cherish him . Love him .

255
00:30:00,244 --> 00:30:02,804
I wouldn 't be here if I didn 't .

256
00:30:03,829 --> 00:30:04,428
